 ---
 
+## Scope decisions
+- [2026-06-21] **Descoped to timing only.** User: "I don't need note or labels. I only
+  care about things like timing." So `set_cue` ships `{ cue, list?, time?, confirm? }`
+  sending `Cue <list> / <cue> Time <t>#` — no label, no notes. This also sidesteps the
+  Label/Note one-line conflict below entirely (only one optional term, `Time`).
+- [2026-06-21] **Why the original Label+Note single line was risky:** `record.go`
+  documents a verified invariant — a cue Label's free text runs to end-of-line, so a
+  `Note` keyword placed after `Label` would be swallowed into the label string. Two
+  free-text fields can't safely share one Eos command line. Moot now that label/notes
+  are out of scope, but recorded for any future label/note editor (use separate command
+  lines, or keep Label strictly last).
+
+---
+
